---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { repository, source } from "../data/project";
const previewSource = source;
const sources = [
  ["claude-code-otel", "Claude Code", "Local runtime · opt-in client configuration", "OTLP import / HTTP"],
  ["claude-cowork-otel", "Claude Cowork", "Cowork runtime · Team / Enterprise admin", "OTLP via reachable collector"],
  ["codex-otel", "Codex", "Local runtime · user or managed OTel config", "OTLP import / HTTP"],
  ["cursor-runtime", "Cursor runtime", "Server-side OTel · Enterprise admin", "OTLP via public HTTPS collector"],
  ["copilot-otel", "Copilot OTel", "Supported client runtime · local / managed config", "OTLP import / HTTP"],
  ["cursor-audit", "Cursor audit", "Team account changes · Enterprise Admin API", "JSON import / API poll"],
  ["copilot-audit", "Copilot audit", "Copilot audit category · audit-read permission", "JSON import / API poll"],
  ["copilot-session", "Copilot session stream", "Request / response records · eligible enterprise preview", "JSON import"],
  ["anthropic-compliance", "Anthropic Compliance", "Activity Feed · enabled API and scoped key", "JSON import / API poll"],
  ["openai-audit", "OpenAI API Platform", "Organization administration · Admin API key", "JSON import / API poll"],
  ["google-gemini", "Gemini in Workspace", "Workspace feature use · authorized Reports API", "JSON import / API poll"],
];
---

<Layout title="Hooks & telemetry — AI Lens" active="telemetry"
  description="Experimental source-build guide to seven native hook adapters and eleven observation-only telemetry sources. Review blocking, setup, privacy, and coverage limits.">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">FIELD GUIDE / 03 · EXPERIMENTAL</p>
      <h1>More sources.<br /><span>Clearer boundaries.</span></h1>
      <p>Request blocking through native pre-tool hooks. Collect runtime telemetry and provider audit records for observation. Choose the integration that answers your question.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <span>ON THIS PAGE</span>
        <a href="#preview">01 / Source build</a>
        <a href="#native">Native hooks / Blocking</a>
        <a href="#sources">02 / Source matrix</a>
        <a href="#ingest">03 / Ingest locally</a>
        <a href="#configure">04 / Review configuration</a>
        <a href="#privacy">05 / Privacy & limits</a>
        <a href="#evidence">06 / Official references</a>
      </aside>
      <div class="docs-content">
        <section class="doc-section" id="preview">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / SOURCE BUILD ONLY</p>
          <h2>Build the integrations locally.</h2>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Start with a source build.</strong>
            <p>The current source includes seven native adapters and eleven telemetry sources. The three newer adapters and telemetry ingestion remain experimental. Cowork Desktop/VM execution remains unvalidated.</p>
          </div>
          <CodeBlock code={`git clone ${repository}.git
cd AI-Lens
cargo build --locked --workspace
./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry sources`} label="Source build · POSIX shell" />
          <p>Build both workspace crates so the CLI has its adjacent engine library. On Windows use the corresponding <code>agent-lens.exe</code> path. The commands do not install client settings.</p>
          <div class="telemetry-kinds">
            <article><span class="integration-label">RUNTIME</span><h3>Requests and tool activity.</h3><p>OTel describes instrumented sessions, requests, timing, and usage. Its coverage follows the producer.</p></article>
            <article><span class="integration-label">PROVIDER AUDIT</span><h3>Account and service activity.</h3><p>Provider feeds describe events within an organization. Administrative logs do not capture every local tool call.</p></article>
            <article><span class="integration-label">NATIVE HOOKS</span><h3>A separate control point.</h3><p>Seven adapters can request denial at supported synchronous pre-tool hooks. OTLP and provider audit ingestion never run block rules.</p></article>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="native">
          <p class="eyebrow">NATIVE HOOKS / SOURCE PREVIEW</p>
          <h2>Block where the client provides a gate.</h2>
          <p>Native adapter IDs are <code>claude</code>, <code>codex</code>, <code>hermes</code>, <code>gemini</code>, <code>cursor</code>, <code>copilot</code>, and <code>cowork</code>. A client must load the hook, invoke it before dispatch, and honor its response. Post-tool and lifecycle matches remain observations.</p>
          <CodeBlock code={`./target/debug/agent-lens --state /absolute/path/lens-state start \\
  --output /absolute/path/events.jsonl --rules /absolute/path/default.yaml
./target/debug/agent-lens --state /absolute/path/lens-state config --agent cursor
./target/debug/agent-lens --state /absolute/path/lens-state config --agent copilot
./target/debug/agent-lens --state /absolute/path/lens-state config --agent cowork`} label="Replace absolute paths · print each integration for review" />
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Cursor: 11 events.</strong> Merge into project or user <code>.cursor/hooks.json</code>, complete workspace trust, and reload/restart as required. Only <code>preToolUse</code> blocks. Generated config sets <code>failClosed: true</code> and a ten-second timeout; normal pre-tool and observational subagent-start responses explicitly allow continuation. Cloud initial read-only turns run no hooks.</li>
            <li><strong>Copilot CLI: 12 events.</strong> Merge into <code>.github/hooks/*.json</code> or user <code>.copilot/hooks/*.json</code>, complete trust, and restart the CLI. Only <code>preToolUse</code> blocks. Direct <code>exec</code>/<code>args</code> configuration is CLI-only; its 30-second timeout <strong>fails open upstream</strong>. It is not an IDE/cloud integration.</li>
            <li><strong>Cowork: five events.</strong> Package generated <code>hooks/hooks.json</code> with a plugin manifest, then install and activate through Desktop's plugin flow. Only <code>PreToolUse</code> blocks; its config requests <code>onFailure: block</code>. Provision the executable/library separately, without top-level <code>bin/</code> or a required skill. Documented plugin support does not establish Desktop/VM execution or path reachability.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Review <a href={previewSource("docs/agents.md")}>complete event registries, installation and failure contracts</a> and the <a href={previewSource("examples/cowork-plugin/README.md")}>Cowork packaging example</a>. Configuration output does not install settings, grant trust, or prove hook invocation. Keep executable, engine, state, rules and output reachable in the actual runtime.</p>
          <p><code>config --agent cursor</code> configures a native gate. <code>telemetry config --source cursor-runtime</code> configures observation. Cowork OTel, Copilot OTel, session streams and provider audit feeds follow that same boundary.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="sources">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / ELEVEN DISTINCT SOURCES</p>
          <h2>Choose the evidence you need.</h2>
          <p>Official contracts checked October 29, 2026. Entitlements and admin permissions apply before a provider can export anything. Each row identifies a specific surface, not complete visibility into a product.</p>
          <div class="telemetry-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Telemetry sources, scroll horizontally on small screens">
            <table>
              <caption>Experimental source inventory and ingest modes</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source / ID</th><th scope="col">Coverage / access</th><th scope="col">Ingest</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>{sources.map(([id, name, scope, input]) => (
                <tr><th scope="row">{name}<code>{id}</code></th><td>{scope}</td><td>{input}</td></tr>
              ))}</tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>Local session folders are a fourth kind of evidence. A documented storage path does not establish a stable export schema. Lens does not crawl Copilot history or assume an IDE transcript format.</p>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Product names are not interchangeable.</strong>
            <p>Cowork has its own monitoring configuration; it does not configure Claude Code or the Code tab. OpenAI API Platform audit logs are separate from Codex OTel. Workspace Gemini activity uses <code>gemini_in_workspace_apps</code>; it is separate from Gemini CLI hooks.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="ingest">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / LOCAL OBSERVATION JSONL</p>
          <h2>Listen, import, or poll.</h2>
          <CodeBlock code={`./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry listen \\
  --source claude-code-otel --bind 127.0.0.1:4318 \\
  --output ./claude-code-telemetry.jsonl`} label="Foreground OTLP listener" />
          <p>The loopback listener accepts OTLP HTTP JSON and protobuf at <code>/v1/logs</code>, <code>/v1/metrics</code>, and <code>/v1/traces</code>. Providers may emit fewer signals. It has no gRPC server, TLS termination, or collector authentication. Use separate ports and files per source; the source label does not authenticate a sender.</p>
          <p>Send HTTP/1.1 POST requests with <code>Content-Length</code>: up to 8 MiB per body, 16 KiB of headers, and a five-second read deadline. Chunked transfer and gzip are unsupported. Configure collector forwarding with compression disabled and a content length. Success follows a locked, synced append; normalized batches are limited to 10,000 events and 32 MiB.</p>
          <CodeBlock code={`./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry import \\
  --source codex-otel --signal logs --format json \\
  --input ./otlp-logs.json --output ./codex-telemetry.jsonl

./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry import \\
  --source copilot-otel --signal traces --format protobuf \\
  --input ./otlp-traces.pb --output ./copilot-telemetry.jsonl`} label="Import authorized OTLP export messages" />
          <p>Provider exports use their documented JSON envelopes or JSONL records. Binary input is an OTLP export message, without a gRPC frame. CSV and arbitrary console output are not accepted contracts.</p>
          <CodeBlock code={`./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry poll --source openai-audit \\
  --token-env OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY --output ./openai-audit.jsonl \\
  --checkpoint ./openai-audit.checkpoint.json --max-pages 10`} label="Bounded read · authorized API Platform organization" />
          <p>Provision the token through your approved secret manager first; <code>--token-env</code> names the variable, not the secret. A poll retrieves a bounded set of pages. It is not a background service or an OAuth login flow. Consult the source guide for account scope, time windows, pagination, and supported polling flags.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="configure">
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / EXPLICIT CONFIGURATION</p>
          <h2>Review before connecting.</h2>
          <CodeBlock code="./target/debug/agent-lens telemetry config --source claude-code-otel" label="Print configuration for review" />
          <p>Review the <a href={previewSource("examples/telemetry/configs")}>configuration templates</a> and merge only the relevant settings manually. Managed policy can override local values. Complete normal client consent and trust steps; Lens does not edit global settings or bypass policy.</p>
          <p>Cowork exports from its VM or cloud runtime. Cursor exports from its servers and requires public HTTPS with authentication. Their loopback address is not your host. Use a reachable, secured collector and forward to Lens on the collector host.</p>
          <p>The <a href={previewSource("examples/telemetry/configs/otel-collector.yaml")}>Collector Contrib example</a> provides TLS/auth ingress and an optional gRPC bridge. Supply real certificates and secrets outside source control, preserve source separation, and validate it against your installed Collector release. It is an example, not a tested production deployment.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="privacy">
          <p class="eyebrow">05 / METADATA FIRST</p>
          <h2>Observe without keeping raw content.</h2>
          <p>Lens keeps an allowlist of metadata and drops raw log bodies, prompts, tool arguments/results, unknown fields, and recognized credential patterns. Output uses <code>agent-lens.telemetry.v1</code> with <code>enforcement: observe_only</code>. A provider approval or denial is that provider's observation, not a Lens block.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Keep source content capture off. Older Cowork versions may export content unless the managed device policy explicitly sets <code>otlpContentCapture</code> to <code>[]</code>.</li>
            <li>Metadata can identify people, sessions, and resources. The allowlist is not a complete anonymizer or DLP system.</li>
            <li>Filtering does not erase content already present in the source file, producer, or collector buffers.</li>
            <li>Allow for batching, delayed events, duplicates, and gaps. Preserve source time and receipt time separately.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Configure output access, retention, rotation, and downstream identity yourself. This preview is not a durable, tamper-evident audit service and does not prove complete agent visibility.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="doc-section" id="evidence">
          <p class="eyebrow">06 / TRACEABLE RESEARCH</p>
          <h2>Follow the provider contracts.</h2>
          <p>The <a href={previewSource("docs/telemetry-sources.md")}>full source guide</a> preserves official URLs, retrieval dates, schemas, permissions, latency and content caveats for all eleven sources. It separates published contracts from local implementation tests.</p>
          <p>Local fixture and receiver tests do not validate enterprise entitlements, managed-policy rollout, live-client delivery, cloud networking, or production reliability. No enterprise live test is claimed for these integrations.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .telemetry-kinds { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .telemetry-kinds article { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--panel); }
  .telemetry-kinds h3 { font-size: 1.06rem; margin-top: .7rem; }
  .telemetry-kinds p { font-size: .9rem; }
  .telemetry-table { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; }
  .telemetry-table:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  table { width: 100%; min-width: 620px; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .87rem; }
  caption { text-align: left; padding: 1rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  thead th { font-size: .75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--muted); }
  tbody th { font-weight: 600; }
  tbody th code { display: block; margin-top: .35rem; font-size: .72rem; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 400; }
  td { color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .telemetry-kinds { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
